  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implementation will be in Go, following existing Hyperledger Fabric SDK patterns for channel configuration.",
    "Will reuse existing config structures (e.g., `config.Organization`) and helper functions for parsing and updating config transactions.",
    "For U8 (certificate revocation), will update the `RevocationList` field in `FabricMSPConfig` using X.509 serial number handling.",
    "All new functions will be designed to integrate with the existing channel configuration API, allowing chaining of updates.",
    "Will use table-driven tests for comprehensive coverage of new functions."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The existing Hyperledger Fabric codebase is available and the developer is familiar with its architecture.",
    "The existing channel configuration API and related structures are stable and well-documented.",
    "Example tests exist for the current API and follow a consistent pattern that can be updated.",
    "No major changes to the underlying protobuf or config structures are required.",
    "The developer has a functioning development environment with Go toolchain and Hyperledger Fabric dependencies.",
    "The revocation list in MSP config is implemented as a list of X.509 certificate serial numbers, which is standard in Hyperledger Fabric."
  ],
